    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9370" root="حنو and حنى" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِيَّةٌ</span></b>  <i>A bow;</i> (T, S, K;) so called because it is
bent: (T:) pl. ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِىٌّ</span></b> , (S, * K,) [or this is a coll.
gen. n., of which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِيَّةٌ</span> is the n. un.,] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنَايَا</span>,
(T, S, K,) or this may be pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَنِىٌّ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
Also applied to <i>A</i> [<i>bowed,</i> or <i>curved,</i>] <i>structure</i>
or <i>building.</i> (M, TA.)

